{"step_index":577,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-16T19:12:52Z","input_tokens":2392,"cache_read_tokens":143216,"output_tokens":17897,"thinking":"Planning the `benchmark_suite.py` script requires two primary approaches for resource sampling. The script must either import the `resource_sampler` module or spawn it as a subprocess to collect resource usage data. Scenarios are conditional on the `--test` flag: `--test 1` runs a baseline test, while `--test thesis_matrix` triggers a more complex set of matrix operations.\n\n\nThe script will systematically execute different scenarios defined by team and container counts. Each scenario starts with a clean environment and baseline resource measurement, followed by team provisioning, container deployment, and setup verification. Resource usage will be monitored throughout these stages. Specifically, the script measures resource consumption before, during, and after the deployment and verification phases, using a sampling process.\n\n\nThe script's execution is structured into six distinct barriers, each timed to isolate resource consumption within specific phases like provisioning, deployment, and teardown. Time windows will be used to analyze resource data. Resource sampling will be parsed and analyzed for each barrier, focusing on CPU, I/O, RAM and ARC usage.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"import argparse\\nimport asyncio\\nimport csv\\nimport json\\nimport logging\\nimport math\\nimport os\\nimport signal\\nimport subprocess\\nimport sys\\nimport time\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\\n\\nimport httpx\\n\\n# Ensure blueagent and tests are importable\\nsys.path.insert(0, '/home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/src')\\nsys.path.insert(0, '/home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent')\\nos.environ['BLUEAGENT_CTFD_API_TOKEN'] = 'secret-token'\\n\\nfrom blueagent.engine.