{"step_index":594,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-16T19:30:35Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-16T21:30:35+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-10-16T21:30:35+02:00\n\nThe command exited with code 0.\nOutput:\n    async def connect_network(\r\n        self,\r\n        instance_name: str,\r\n        network_name: str,\r\n        ip_address: Optional[str] = None,\r\n    ) -> None:\r\n        \"\"\"Attaches the instance's eth0 NIC to an OVN or bridge network.\"\"\"\r\n        eth0_config: Dict[str, str] = {\r\n            \"type\": \"nic\",\r\n            \"network\": network_name,\r\n            \"parent\": \"\",  # Clear prior host bridge binding when transitioning to OVN\r\n        }\r\n        if ip_address:\r\n            eth0_config[\"ipv4.address\"] = ip_address\r\n\r\n        device_patch = {\r\n            \"devices\": {\r\n                \"eth0\": eth0_config,\r\n            }\r\n        }\r\n        res = await self.client.patch(f\"instances/{instance_name}\", json=device_patch)\r\n        if res.status_code >= 400:\r\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"Failed to connect instance '{instance_name}' to network '{network_name}' ({res.status_code}): {res.text}\")\r\n\r\n        op = res.json().get(\"operation\")\r\n        if op:\r\n\n"}
{"step_index":595,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-16T19:30:35Z","input_tokens":2673,"cache_read_tokens":171366,"output_tokens":987,"thinking":"In the `connect_network` function, the IP address is not explicitly provided, causing the OVN driver to dynamically assign one from its pool to the cloned network instance. Recalling the network configuration for `verify-{self.team_k}`, the previously set IPv4 address needs to be reviewed.\n\n\nIf an IP address is not explicitly provided during network connection, dynamic allocation from the OVN subnet occurs. The device configuration created during the initial challenge deployment does *not* predefine the IP. The `connect_network` operation includes an IP address, the system can statically bind the calculated address, circumventing dynamic allocation and reducing the chance of transaction lock collisions. Dynamic allocation failures could result from these transaction locks during concurrent network creation.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"ssh debian@192.168.0.199 \\\"sed -n '70,85p' /home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/src/blueagent/verifier/ovn.py\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/scratch\"","IsDaemon":"false","RunPersistent":"false","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Checking connect_network in ovn.py\"","toolSummary":"\"Check ovn.py connect_network call\""}}]}
