{"step_index":633,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-16T19:54:26Z","input_tokens":2397,"cache_read_tokens":216437,"output_tokens":1505,"content":"I have completed the redesign of the benchmark suite, executed all tests, and gathered complete timing, CPU, and RAM telemetry across both **Alpine Linux** and **Ubuntu Heavy** containers.\n\nA detailed summary is documented in [walkthrough.md](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/walkthrough.md), and all findings are compiled in your dedicated thesis notes file: [thesis_notes.md](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/thesis_notes.md) (also available on the server at `/home/debian/bluectfd/thesis_notes.md`).\n\n---\n\n### Key Architectural & Empirical Findings for Your Thesis\n\n1. **ZFS Copy-on-Write (CoW) Speedup Factor ($1.3\\times \\to 3.6\\times$):**\n   - At high multi-tenant scale ($M=10$ teams, $N=5$ containers, 100 peak containers running simultaneously), cold container deployment (`Deploy Create`) rose to **76.19 seconds** on Ubuntu Heavy.\n   - In contrast, ZFS snapshot cloning (`CoW Clone`) during verification took only **22.17 seconds**—a **$3.44\\times$ speedup** on Ubuntu Heavy and **$3.60\\times$ speedup** on Alpine.\n   - This proves that ZFS snapshot cloning is an $O(1)$ block-pointer metadata operation that remains near-constant regardless of whether the rootfs is 3.2 MB (Alpine) or 1.5 GB (Ubuntu).\n\n2. **Memory Density & Host Capacity:**\n   - **Alpine Linux:** Idles at **~15.3 MB/container** at 100-container scale (+1,533 MB net delta).\n   - **Ubuntu Heavy:** Idles at **~52.5 MB/container** at 100-container scale (+5,247 MB net delta) while running full `systemd`, `nginx`, `postgresql-16`, and `python3`.\n   - All 100 concurrent Ubuntu containers consumed only **9.23 GiB** host RAM with **zero swap thrashing** on your 15 GiB host.\n\n3. **CPU Utilization Profile:**\n   - Measured via the dedicated 100ms subprocess sampler reading `/proc/stat`.\n   - Peak CPU during deployment reached **23.1%** for Ubuntu Heavy vs. **19.7%** for Alpine. The extra overhead is driven by parallel `systemd` daemon initialization rather than c\n<truncated 189 bytes>\neasurement of the time to start verification and ensured all 100 containers were active at rest simultaneously.\n   - Binding static IPv4 addresses directly during OVN network attachment eliminated dynamic pool lock contention, achieving a **100% pass rate** across all 18 scenarios.\n\n---\n\n### Generated Datasets for Thesis Plotting\n\nAll files are preserved on the remote server (`/home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/tests/`) and synchronized to your local workspace:\n\n- **Alpine Datasets:**\n  - [thesis_alpine_results.csv](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/thesis_alpine_results.csv) (Summary rows for master tables)\n  - [thesis_alpine_step_resources.csv](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/thesis_alpine_step_resources.csv) (108 long-format step resource rows for bar/line charts)\n  - [thesis_alpine_timeseries.csv](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/thesis_alpine_timeseries.csv) (8,634 raw 100ms samples for continuous timeline plots)\n  - [thesis_alpine_report.md](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/thesis_alpine_report.md)\n- **Ubuntu Heavy Datasets:**\n  - [thesis_ubuntu_results.csv](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/thesis_ubuntu_results.csv) (Summary rows for master tables)\n  - [thesis_ubuntu_step_resources.csv](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/thesis_ubuntu_step_resources.csv) (108 long-format step resource rows for bar/line charts)\n  - [thesis_ubuntu_timeseries.csv](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/thesis_ubuntu_timeseries.csv) (10,833 raw 100ms samples for continuous timeline plots)\n  - [thesis_ubuntu_report.md](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/thesis_ubuntu_report.md)","truncated_fields":["content"]}
